                  %a{:href => "#ModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"} Model structure on compactly generated topological spaces
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#pointed_compactly_generated_topological_spaces"} Pointed compactly generated topological spaces
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#compactly_generated_weakly_hausdorff_spaces"} Compactly generated weakly Hausdorff spaces
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#TopologicalEnrichment"} Monoidal and topologically enriched model structure
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ModelStructureOnTopEnrichedFunctors"} The model structure on topologically enriched functors
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em classical model structure on topological spaces
            or
            %em Quillen-Serre model structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
            (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67, II.3
            ) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            (also on many
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+categories+of+topological+spaces"} convenient categories of topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"}> topological homotopy theory
            ), in that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category of a model category
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
            on
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complexes"} cell complexes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
          %p
            Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
            are the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibrations"} Serre fibrations
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
          %p
            The
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} adjunction
            constitutes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "homotopy+hypothesis#ForKanComplexes"} for Kan complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            this means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            both are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
          %p
            There are also other model structures on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            itself, see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} model structure on topological spaces
            for more. This entry here focuses on just the classical model structure on topological spaces.
          %h2#background_from_pointset_topology Background from point-set topology
          %p
            This section recalls basic relevant concepts from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            (“point-set topology”) and highlights some basic facts that may serve to motivate the Quillen model structure below.
          %h3#homotopy Homotopy
          %p
            The fundamental concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            this is about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} contiunous
            deformations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            parameterized by the standard
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+interval"} topological interval
          #TopologicalInterval.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I \coloneqq [0,1] \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %p
              for the standard
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+interval"} topological interval
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            %p Equipped with the canonical inclusion of its two endpoints
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi I
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∃
                        %mo !
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ast \sqcup \ast \stackrel{(\delta_0,\delta_1)}{\longrightarrow} I \stackrel{\exists !}{\longrightarrow} \ast
            %p
              this is the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Top
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times I
              is called the standard
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\nabla_X
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X \sqcup X
                    \\stackrel{((id,\delta_0),(id,\delta_1))}{\longrightarrow}
                    X \times I
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X
                    \\,.
          #LeftHomotopy.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g\colon X \longrightarrow Y
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi L
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow_L g
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; X \times I \longrightarrow Y
            %p
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the standard interval of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalInterval"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id,\delta_0)}}\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    X \times I &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(id,\delta_1)}}\uparrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
          #HomotopyEquivalence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Y
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              if there exists a continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \longleftarrow Y \;\colon\; g
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopies"} left homotopies
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta_1 \;\colon\; f\circ g \Rightarrow_L id_Y
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta_2 \;\colon\; g\circ f \Rightarrow_L id_X
                    \\,.
            %p
              If here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_2
              is constant along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is is said to exhibit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retract"} deformation retract
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            Another key application of the concept of left homotopy is to the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
          #HomotopyGroupsOftopologicalSpaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(X)
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 0-th homotopy set
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              of points
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              this extends to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_0 \colon Top \longrightarrow Set
                    \\,.
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon \ast \to X
              any point, then the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
