          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              says, in view of the definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a map with the property that given a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
              Therefore the condition on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              is also called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
              for maps whose domain is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-disk"} n-disk
            %p
              More generally one may ask functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              to have such
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
              for functions with arbitrary domain. These are called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibrations"} Hurewicz fibrations
          #SerreFibrationsByLiftingAgainstMapsHomeomorphicToDiskInclusions.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
