              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n \times I
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              turns out not to actually matter much for the nature of Serre fibrations. We will eventually find below (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingPropertyInTheClassicalModelStructureOnTopologicalSpaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n \hookrightarrow D^n \times I
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
              and that all of these may be generated from them in a suitable way.
            %p
              But for simple special cases this is readily seen directly, too. Notably it is trivial, but nevertheless important in applications, that we could replace the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-disks"} n-disks
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              with any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              topological space. A choice that becomes important in the comparison to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              is to instead take the topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-simplices"} n-simplices
