          #CofibrantGenerationOfPointedTopologicalSpaces.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The classes in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingCofibrationsForPointedTopologicalSpaces"}
              exhibit the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Quillen
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{Quillen}
              as a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
          %p
            This is a special case of a general statement about cofibrant generation of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coslice+model+structures"} coslice model structures
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+an+over+category#ModelStructureInheritsGoodProperties"} this proposition
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_15 Proof
            %p
              Due to the fact that in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top^{\ast/}}
              a basepoint is freely adjoined, lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations"}
              goes through verbatim for the pointed case, with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
              replaced by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Top
                            %mrow
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top^{\ast/}}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
              and lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JTopRelativeCellComplexesAreWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
              %a{:href => "#VerificationOfTopQuillen"} above
              in the proof of theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
          %h3#ModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces Model structure on compactly generated topological spaces
          %p
            The category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            has the technical inconvenience that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^Y
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactOpenTopology"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
            but fail to exist more generally. In other words:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            is not
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
                is
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative"} associative
            %li
              %p
                there is a concept of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+functors"} topologically enriched functors
                with values in topological spaces, to which we turn
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#ModelStructureOnTopEnrichedFunctors"} below
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                preserves
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
          %p
            Now, since, by the above, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of topological spaces only cares about the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+approximation"} CW approximation
            to any topological space, it is plausible to ask for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            which still contains all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
          %p
            Such a full subcategory exists, the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
          #kTop.num_defn
            %h6#definition_21 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %p
              A subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset X
              is called
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                \-closed
              if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon K \longrightarrow X
              out of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{-1}(A)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated
              if its closed subsets exhaust (hence coincide with) the
              = succeed "-closed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Top_{cg} \hookrightarrow Top
            %p
              for the
