                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \times A \overset{(id,f)}{\longrightarrow} \emptyset \times B
              is an isomorphism, and so the pushout in the pushout product is
              = succeed "." do
