                    \\array{
                    \&amp; I_{Top} \Box I_{Top} &amp; \text{has LLP against} &amp; W_{cl} \cap Fib_{cl}
                    \\\
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \&amp; I_{Top} &amp; \text{has LLP against} &amp; (W_{cl} \cap Fib_{cl})^{\Box I_{Top}}
                    \\\
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \&amp; Cof_{cl} &amp; \text{has LLP against} &amp; (W_{cl} \cap Fib_{cl})^{\Box I_{Top}}
                    \\\
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \&amp;
                    I_{Top} \Box Cof_{cl} &amp; \text{has LLP against} &amp; W_{cl} \cap Fib_{cl}
                    \\\
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \&amp;
                    I_{Top} &amp; \text{has LLP against} &amp; (W_{cl} \cap Fib_{cl})^{Cof_{cl}}
                    \\\
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \&amp; Cof_{cl} &amp; \text{has LLP against} &amp; (W_{cl} \cap Fib_{cl})^{Cof_{cl}}
                    \\\
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \&amp; Cof_{cl} \Box \Cof_{cl}  &amp; \text{has LLP against} &amp; W_{cl} \cap Fib_{cl}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where all logical equivalences used are those of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JoyalTierneyCalculus"}
              and where all implications appearing are by the closure property of lifting problems (
              %a{:href => "injective+or+projective+morphism#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}> prop.
              ).
            %p
              Regarding the second point: By example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProductOfITopwithITopAndJTop"}
              we moreover have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi Top
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi Top
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_{Top} \Box J_{Top} \subset J_{Top}
            %p and the conclusion follows by the same kind of reasoning.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_8 Remark
            %p
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              theory the property in proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProductInTopCGSendsCofCofToCof"}
              is referred to as saying that the model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
              from theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureOnTopcg"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
                  with respect to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                  on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Top
                            %mi cg
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
              %li
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
          %p A key point of what this entails is the following:
          #HomProductAdjunctionForCofibrantObjectInTopCGIsQuillen.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_20 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
              cofibrant (a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell complex
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianClosureOfTopcg"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
                    \\underoverset
                    \\underset{(-)^X}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\overset{X \times (-)}{\longleftarrow}
                    {\bot}
                    (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_26 Proof
            %p
              By example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProductWithInitialMorphism"}
              we have that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              functor is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+product"} pushout product
              functor with the initial morphism of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo □
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \times (-)
                    \\simeq
                    (\emptyset \to X) \Box (-)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By assumption
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\emptyset \to X)
              is a cofibration, and hence prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProductInTopCGSendsCofCofToCof"}
              says that this is a left Quillen functor.
          %p
            The statement and proof of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomProductAdjunctionForCofibrantObjectInTopCGIsQuillen"}
            has a direct analogue in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
          #HomProductAdjunctionForCofibrantObjectInPointedTopCGIsQuillen.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_21 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}
              cofibrant with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              (theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureOnSliceCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell complex
              with non-degenerate basepoint, remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonDegenerateBasepointAsCofibrantObjects"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashHomAdjunctionOnPointedCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              (def.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunction"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}
                    \\underoverset
                    \\underset{(-)^X}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\overset{X \times (-)}{\longleftarrow}
                    {\bot}
                    (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_27 Proof
            %p
              Let now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo □
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box_\wedge
              denote the
              %strong smash pushout product
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo □
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{\Box(-)}
              the
              %strong smash pullback powering
              defined as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProduct"}
              and def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PullbackPowering"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              replaced by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashProductOfPointedObjects"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              replaced by pointed mapping spaces (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointedMappingSpace"}
            %p
              By theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantGenerationOfPointedTopologicalSpaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top_{cg}^{\ast/})_{Quillen}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi Top
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top^{\ast/}} = (I_{Top})_+
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Top
                            %mrow
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top^{\ast/}}= (J_{Top})_+
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeAndSmashOfBasePointAdjoinedTopologicalSpaces"}
              gives that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_n \in I_{Top}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_n \in J_{Top}
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo □
                      %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i_{n_1})_+ \Box_\wedge (i_{n_2})_+ \simeq (i_{n_1 + n_2})_+
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i_{n_1})_+ \wedge_\wedge (i_{n_2})_+ \simeq (i_{n_1 + n_2})_+
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the pointed analog of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProductInTopCGSendsCofCofToCof"}
              holds and therefore so does the pointed analog of the conclusion in prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomProductAdjunctionForCofibrantObjectInTopCGIsQuillen"}
          %h3#ModelStructureOnTopEnrichedFunctors The model structure on topologically enriched functors
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+enriched+functors"} projective model structure on enriched functors
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza91"} Piacenza 91
          %p
            In the following we say
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"}> Top
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"}> Top
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            etc. for what often is referred to as “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+category"}> topological category
            ” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+functor"}> topological functor
            ” etc. As discussed there, these latter terms are ambiguous.
          #TopEnrichedCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_27 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+category"} topologically enriched category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Obj
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(\mathcal{C})
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %strong
                      class of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b\in Obj(\mathcal{C})
                  a topological space
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Top
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{C}(a,b)\in Top
                        \\,,
                %p
                  called the
                  %strong
                    space of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  or the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-space"} hom-space
                  between
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b,c\in Obj(\mathcal{C})
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∘
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\circ_{a,b,c} \;\colon\; \mathcal{C}(a,b)\times \mathcal{C}(b,c) \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}(a,c)
                %p
                  out of the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  operation
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in Obj(\mathcal{C})
                  a point
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Id
                            %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_a\in \mathcal{C}(a,a)
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
                  morphism on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %p
              such that the composition is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unital
            %p
              Similarly a
              %strong pointed topologically enriched category
              is such a structire with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_k
              replaced by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
              and with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              replaced by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of pointed topological spaces.
          #UnderlyingCategoryOfTopEnrichedCategory.num_remark
            %h6#remark_9 Remark
            %p
              Given a (pointed)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+category"} topologically enriched category
              as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopEnrichedCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
              (along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi k
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon Top_k \to Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(a,b) = U(\mathcal{C}(a,b))
                    \\,.
            %p
              It is in this sense that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a category with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
          %p The archetypical example is the following:
          #TopkAsATopologicallyEnrichedCategory.num_example
            %h6#example_14 Example
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Top_k \hookrightarrow Top
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              on the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)\times (-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Top_k \times Top_k \longrightarrow Top_k
            %p
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)^{(-)}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Top_k^{op}\times Top_k
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Top_k
            %p
              this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              (see at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category of topological spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+category"} topologically enriched category
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopEnrichedCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
              given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Top_k(X,Y)
                    \\coloneqq
                    Y^X
            %p
              and with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Y^X \times Z^Y
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Z^X
            %p
              given by the (product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              mapping-space)-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+morphism"} evaluation morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ev
                        %mo ,
                        %mi id
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ev
                    %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \times Y^X \times Z^Y
                    \\overset{(ev, id)}{\longrightarrow}
                    Y \times Z^Y
                    \\overset{ev}{\longrightarrow}
                    Z
                    \\,.
            %p
              Similarly,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
